      "description": "Statues found at Kerma. Identification of pharaohs : 1 and 3. Tanoutamon (664-656), 25th dynasty, H. 196 and 213 cm; 2. Taharqo (or Taharqa, 690-664), 25th dynasty, H 255 cm; 4. Anlamani, king of Napata, H 176 cm; 5. Senkamanisken, king of Napata, H 146 cm. Statues from the cache of Doukki Gel. These statues were discovered, broken, in a cache located between the main temples of the Napatan era. Kerma Museum. Ref. : François-Xavier Fauvelle (dir.), L'Afrique ancienne : de l'Accacus au Zimbabwe. 20 000 avant notre ère - XVIIe siècle, ISBN 978-2-7011-9836-1, p. 76.",
